          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.5.29+LUK.5.30"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lk 5.29-30",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.19.7"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "19.7",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Now the tax collectors and sinners were all drawing near to hear him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the Pharisees and the scribes murmured, saying, “This man receives sinners and eats with them.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So he told them this parable: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "MAT.18.10+MAT.18.11+MAT.18.12+MAT.18.13+MAT.18.14"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Mt 18.10-14",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " “What man of you, having a hundred sheep, if he has lost one of them, does not leave the ninety-nine in the wilderness, and go after the one which is lost, until he finds it? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he has found it, he lays it on his shoulders, rejoicing. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he comes home, he calls together his friends and his neighbors, saying to them, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my sheep which was lost.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JAS.5.20"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Jas 5.20",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.19.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lk 19.10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LUK.15.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "15.10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Just so, I tell you, there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous persons who need no repentance.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Or what woman, having ten silver coins,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15.8",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "The drachma, rendered here by",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "silver coin,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "was about a day's wage for a laborer",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " if she loses one coin, does not light a lamp and sweep the house and seek diligently until she finds it? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when she has found it, she calls together her friends and neighbors, saying, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found the coin which I had lost.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Just so, I tell you, there is joy before the angels of God over one sinner who repents.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "MAT.21.28"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Mt 21.28",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And he said, “There was a man who had two sons; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "DEU.21.15+DEU.21.16+DEU.21.17"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Deut 21.15-17",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and the younger of them said to his father, ‘Father, give me the share of property that falls to me.’ And he divided his living between them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Not many days later, the younger son gathered all he had and took his journey into a far country, and there he squandered his property in loose living. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he had spent everything, a great famine arose in that country, and he began to be in want. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So he went and joined himself to one of the citizens of that country, who sent him into his fields to feed swine. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he would gladly have fed on",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15.16",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Other ancient authorities read",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "filled his belly with",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " the pods that the swine ate; and no one gave him anything. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when he came to himself he said, ‘How many of my father's hired servants have bread enough and to spare, but I perish here with hunger! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will arise and go to my father, and I will say to him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and before you; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I am no longer worthy to be called your son; treat me as one of your hired servants.” ’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he arose and came to his father. But while he was yet at a distance, his father saw him and had compassion, and ran and embraced him and kissed him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the son said to him, ‘Father, I have sinned against heaven and before you; I am no longer worthy to be called your son.’",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15.21",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Other ancient authorities add",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "treat me as one of your hired servants",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "GEN.41.42"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Gen 41.42",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ZEC.3.4"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Zech 3.4",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " But the father said to his servants, ‘Bring quickly the best robe, and put it on him; and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and bring the fatted calf and kill it, and let us eat and make merry; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.15.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.15.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 15:24"
          },
          "items": [
